d HTML for the contents of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<code>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"codehighlightoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeHighlightOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contains optional raw fence "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlightLines"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":" passed to a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeHighlighter"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"headinganchoroptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HeadingAnchorOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configures anchor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaHidden"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabIndex"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"extension-contracts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extension contracts"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"markdownextension","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownExtension"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Named hook object with optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseBlock"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformDocument"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformInline"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderHtml"},{"type":"text","value":" functions, plus an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inlineParser"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"blockparsecontext","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BlockParseContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides source "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lines"},{"type":"text","value":", current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index"},{"type":"text","value":", active "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":", nested "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseInline"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseBlocks"},{"type":"text","value":" helpers, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"consume"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"inlineparser","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InlineParser"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contains literal starting UTF-16 code-unit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markers"},{"type":"text","value":" and a synchronous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parse(context)"},{"type":"text","value":" callback returning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InlineParseResult | undefined"},{"type":"text","value":". Runs at matching source positions after escapes and code spans, before other built-in inline rules."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"inlineparsecontext","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InlineParseContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides current-container "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":", UTF-16 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index"},{"type":"text","value":", active "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inLink"},{"type":"text","value":", and a nested "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseInline(value)"},{"type":"text","value":" helper that shares the recursion and scan budget."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"inlineparseresult","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InlineParseResult"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contains one standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InlineNode"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node"},{"type":"text","value":" and a positive integer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"length"},{"type":"text","value":" in UTF-16 code units. The range must fit in the current source. Invalid lengths throw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RangeError"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"inlinetransformcontext","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InlineTransformContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides active parse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" to inline transforms."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"documenttransformcontext","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DocumentTransformContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides active parse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" to document transforms."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"htmlrendercontext","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HtmlRenderContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides active render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" and recursive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderBlock"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderInline"},{"type":"text","value":" functions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"supporting-data","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supporting data"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"markdownheading","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownHeading"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Collected heading data with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":", numeric "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"level"},{"type":"text","value":", and optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"linkreferencedefinition","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinkReferenceDefinition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normalized reference data with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"href"},{"type":"text","value":" and optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"footnotedefinition","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FootnoteDefinition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Footnote source data with original "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"label"},{"type":"text","value":", Markdown "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", and optional generated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"types","text":"Types","level":1},{"id":"documents-and-unions","text":"Documents and unions","level":2},{"id":"markdowninput","text":"MarkdownInput","level":3},{"id":"markdowndocument","text":"MarkdownDocument","level":3},{"id":"blocknode","text":"BlockNode","level":3},{"id":"inlinenode","text":"InlineNode","level":3},{"id":"block-nodes","text":"Block nodes","level":2},{"id":"headingnode","text":"HeadingNode","level":3},{"id":"paragraphnode","text":"ParagraphNode","level":3},{"id":"codeblocknode","text":"CodeBlockNode","level":3},{"id":"listnode","text":"ListNode","level":3},{"id":"listitemnode","text":"ListItemNode","level":3},{"id":"blockquotenode","text":"BlockquoteNode","level":3},{"id":"tablenode","text":"TableNode","level":3},{"id":"tablecellnode","text":"TableCellNode","level":3},{"id":"footnotesnode","text":"FootnotesNode","level":3},{"id":"footnoteitemnode","text":"FootnoteItemNode","level":3},{"id":"thematicbreaknode","text":"ThematicBreakNode","level":3},{"id":"htmlblocknode","text":"HtmlBlockNode","level":3},{"id":"calloutnode","text":"CalloutNode","level":3},{"id":"componentnode","text":"ComponentNode","level":3},{"id":"inline-nodes","text":"Inline nodes","level":2},{"id":"textnode","text":"TextNode","level":3},{"id":"codespannode","text":"CodeSpanNode","level":3},{"id":"strongnode","text":"StrongNode","level":3},{"id":"emphasisnode","text":"EmphasisNode","level":3},{"id":"strikenode","text":"StrikeNode","level":3},{"id":"footnotereferencenode","text":"FootnoteReferenceNode","level":3},{"id":"linknode","text":"LinkNode","level":3},{"id":"imagenode","text":"ImageNode","level":3},{"id":"breaknode","text":"BreakNode","level":3},{"id":"htmlinlinenode","text":"HtmlInlineNode","level":3},{"id":"inlinecomponentnode","text":"InlineComponentNode","level":3},{"id":"parsing-and-rendering-options","text":"Parsing and rendering options","level":2},{"id":"parseoptions","text":"ParseOptions","level":3},{"id":"urltransform","text":"UrlTransform","level":3},{"id":"renderoptions","text":"RenderOptions","level":3},{"id":"codehighlighter","text":"CodeHighlighter","level":3},{"id":"codehighlightoptions","text":"CodeHighlightOptions","level":3},{"id":"headinganchoroptions","text":"HeadingAnchorOptions","level":3},{"id":"extension-contracts","text":"Extension contracts","level":2},{"id":"markdownextension","text":"MarkdownExtension","level":3},{"id":"blockparsecontext","text":"BlockParseContext","level":3},{"id":"inlineparser","text":"InlineParser","level":3},{"id":"inlineparsecontext","text":"InlineParseContext","level":3},{"id":"inlineparseresult","text":"InlineParseResult","level":3},{"id":"inlinetransformcontext","text":"InlineTransformContext","level":3},{"id":"documenttransformcontext","text":"DocumentTransformContext","level":3},{"id":"htmlrendercontext","text":"HtmlRenderContext","level":3},{"id":"supporting-data","text":"Supporting data","level":2},{"id":"markdownheading","text":"MarkdownHeading","level":3},{"id":"linkreferencedefinition","text":"LinkReferenceDefinition","level":3},{"id":"footnotedefinition","text":"FootnoteDefinition","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Types\n\nAll shared types are exported from `@tanstack/markdown`.\n\n## Documents and unions\n\n### `MarkdownInput`\n\n`string | MarkdownDocument`. Accepted by the complete-document renderers.\n\n### `MarkdownDocument`\n\nThe root object with `type: 'root'`, `children: BlockNode[]`, optional raw `frontmatter`, and optional collected `headings`.\n\n### `BlockNode`\n\nUnion of `HeadingNode`, `ParagraphNode`, `CodeBlockNode`, `ListNode`, `BlockquoteNode`, `TableNode`, `FootnotesNode`, `ThematicBreakNode`, `HtmlBlockNode`, `CalloutNode`, and `ComponentNode`.\n\n### `InlineNode`\n\nUnion of `TextNode`, `CodeSpanNode`, `StrongNode`, `EmphasisNode`, `StrikeNode`, `FootnoteReferenceNode`, `LinkNode`, `ImageNode`, `BreakNode`, `HtmlInlineNode`, and `InlineComponentNode`.\n\n## Block nodes\n\n### `HeadingNode`\n\nContains `depth` from 1 through 6, optional `id` and `framework`, and inline `children`.\n\n### `ParagraphNode`\n\nContains inline `children`.\n\n### `CodeBlockNode`\n\nContains raw `value` plus optional `lang`, `meta`, `title`, `file`, `framework`, and `highlightLines` metadata.\n\n### `ListNode`\n\nContains `ordered`, optional `start`, optional `loose`, and `items: ListItemNode[]`. A true `loose` value preserves paragraph wrappers in every item.\n\n### `ListItemNode`\n\nContains block `children` and optional task-list `checked` state.\n\n### `BlockquoteNode`\n\nContains nested block `children`.\n\n### `TableNode`\n\nContains per-column `align`, a `header`, and body `rows` made from `TableCellNode` values.\n\n### `TableCellNode`\n\nContains inline `children`.\n\n### `FootnotesNode`\n\nGenerated document block containing `items: FootnoteItemNode[]`.\n\n### `FootnoteItemNode`\n\nContains a collision-safe `id`, display `number`, optional `referenceCount`, and block `children`.\n\n### `ThematicBreakNode`\n\nMarker node with `type: 'thematicBreak'`.\n\n### `HtmlBlockNode`\n\nContains raw HTML `value`. It is created only when HTML parsing is enabled.\n\n### `CalloutNode`\n\nContains a callout `kind`, display `title`, and block `children`. It is produced by the callouts extension.\n\n### `ComponentNode`\n\nContains source `name`, parsed `attributes`, block `children`, and optional rendered `tagName` and string `properties`. Docs transforms use it for tabs and framework panels.\n\n## Inline nodes\n\n### `TextNode`\n\nContains plain text `value`.\n\n### `CodeSpanNode`\n\nContains inline code `value`.\n\n### `StrongNode`\n\nContains inline `children` rendered as strong text.\n\n### `EmphasisNode`\n\nContains inline `children` rendered as emphasized text.\n\n### `StrikeNode`\n\nContains inline `children` rendered as deleted text.\n\n### `FootnoteReferenceNode`\n\nContains normalized footnote `id`, display `number`, and optional `referenceIndex` for repeated references.\n\n### `LinkNode`\n\nContains policy-processed `href`, optional `title`, and inline `children`.\n\n### `ImageNode`\n\nContains policy-processed `src`, text `alt`, and optional `title`.\n\n### `BreakNode`\n\nMarker node with `type: 'break'`.\n\n### `HtmlInlineNode`\n\nContains raw inline HTML `value`. It is created only when HTML parsing is enabled.\n\n### `InlineComponentNode`\n\nContains `type: 'inlineComponent'`, `name`, source `attributes`, inline `children`, and optional rendered `tagName` and string `properties`. Uses the same component replacements as `ComponentNode`, with a `<span>` fallback when no tag is provided. See [Custom components](../guides/extensions.md#custom-components).\n\n## Parsing and rendering options\n\n### `ParseOptions`\n\nConfigures `allowHtml`, `urlTransform`, `frontmatter`, `headingIds`, and `extensions`. It also exposes `references`, `footnotes`, `footnoteOrder`, and `footnoteCounts` state used by nested parser contexts.\n\n### `UrlTransform`\n\nSynchronous callback `(url: string, kind: 'link' | 'image', defaultUrl: string) => string | null`. Return the default screened URL, a trusted replacement, or `null` to keep only the label content. Applies during Markdown parsing, not to raw HTML or supplied ASTs. See [Custom URL policy](../core-concepts/security.md#custom-url-policy).\n\n### `RenderOptions`\n\nExtends `ParseOptions` with `highlighter`, `codeLineNumbers`, and `headingAnchors`.\n\n### `CodeHighlighter`\n\nSynchronous callback `(code, lang?, options?) => string`. The returned string is trusted HTML for the contents of `<code>`.\n\n### `CodeHighlightOptions`\n\nContains optional raw fence `meta`, `highlightLines`, and `lineNumbers` passed to a `CodeHighlighter`.\n\n### `HeadingAnchorOptions`\n\nConfigures anchor `content`, `className`, `ariaHidden`, and `tabIndex`.\n\n## Extension contracts\n\n### `MarkdownExtension`\n\nNamed hook object with optional `parseBlock`, `transformDocument`, `transformInline`, and `renderHtml` functions, plus an optional `inlineParser`.\n\n### `BlockParseContext`\n\nProvides source `lines`, current `index`, active `options`, nested `parseInline` and `parseBlocks` helpers, and `consume`.\n\n### `InlineParser`\n\nContains literal starting UTF-16 code-unit `markers` and a synchronous `parse(context)` callback returning `InlineParseResult | undefined`. Runs at matching source positions after escapes and code spans, before other built-in inline rules.\n\n### `InlineParseContext`\n\nProvides current-container `source`, UTF-16 `index`, active `options`, `inLink`, and a nested `parseInline(value)` helper that shares the recursion and scan budget.\n\n### `InlineParseResult`\n\nContains one standard `InlineNode` as `node` and a positive integer `length` in UTF-16 code units. The range must fit in the current source. Invalid lengths throw `RangeError`.\n\n### `InlineTransformContext`\n\nProvides active parse `options` to inline transforms.\n\n### `DocumentTransformContext`\n\nProvides active parse `options` to document transforms.\n\n### `HtmlRenderContext`\n\nProvides active render `options` and recursive `renderBlock` and `renderInline` functions.\n\n## Supporting data\n\n### `MarkdownHeading`\n\nCollected heading data with `id`, `text`, numeric `level`, and optional `framework`.\n\n### `LinkReferenceDefinition`\n\nNormalized reference data with `href` and optional `title`.\n\n### `FootnoteDefinition`\n\nFootnote source data with original `label`, Markdown `content`, and optional generated `id`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Types\n---\n\n# Types\n\nAll shared types are exported from `@tanstack/markdown`.\n\n## Documents and unions\n\n### `MarkdownInput`\n\n`string | MarkdownDocument`. Accepted by the complete-document renderers.\n\n### `MarkdownDocument`\n\nThe root object with `type: 'root'`, `children: BlockNode[]`, optional raw `frontmatter`, and optional collected `headings`.\n\n### `BlockNode`\n\nUnion of `HeadingNode`, `ParagraphNode`, `CodeBlockNode`, `ListNode`, `BlockquoteNode`, `TableNode`, `FootnotesNode`, `ThematicBreakNode`, `HtmlBlockNode`, `CalloutNode`, and `ComponentNode`.\n\n### `InlineNode`\n\nUnion of `TextNode`, `CodeSpanNode`, `StrongNode`, `EmphasisNode`, `StrikeNode`, `FootnoteReferenceNode`, `LinkNode`, `ImageNode`, `BreakNode`, `HtmlInlineNode`, and `InlineComponentNode`.\n\n## Block nodes\n\n### `HeadingNode`\n\nContains `depth` from 1 through 6, optional `id` and `framework`, and inline `children`.\n\n### `ParagraphNode`\n\nContains inline `children`.\n\n### `CodeBlockNode`\n\nContains raw `value` plus optional `lang`, `meta`, `title`, `file`, `framework`, and `highlightLines` metadata.\n\n### `ListNode`\n\nContains `ordered`, optional `start`, optional `loose`, and `items: ListItemNode[]`. A true `loose` value preserves paragraph wrappers in every item.\n\n### `ListItemNode`\n\nContains block `children` and optional task-list `checked` state.\n\n### `BlockquoteNode`\n\nContains nested block `children`.\n\n### `TableNode`\n\nContains per-column `align`, a `header`, and body `rows` made from `TableCellNode` values.\n\n### `TableCellNode`\n\nContains inline `children`.\n\n### `FootnotesNode`\n\nGenerated document block containing `items: FootnoteItemNode[]`.\n\n### `FootnoteItemNode`\n\nContains a collision-safe `id`, display `number`, optional `referenceCount`, and block `children`.\n\n### `ThematicBreakNode`\n\nMarker node with `type: 'thematicBreak'`.\n\n### `HtmlBlockNode`\n\nContains raw HTML `value`. It is created only when HTML parsing is enabled.\n\n### `CalloutNode`\n\nContains a callout `kind`, display `title`, and block `children`. It is produced by the callouts extension.\n\n### `ComponentNode`\n\nContains source `name`, parsed `attributes`, block `children`, and optional rendered `tagName` and string `properties`. Docs transforms use it for tabs and framework panels.\n\n## Inline nodes\n\n### `TextNode`\n\nContains plain text `value`.\n\n### `CodeSpanNode`\n\nContains inline code `value`.\n\n### `StrongNode`\n\nContains inline `children` rendered as strong text.\n\n### `EmphasisNode`\n\nContains inline `children` rendered as emphasized text.\n\n### `StrikeNode`\n\nContains inline `children` rendered as deleted text.\n\n### `FootnoteReferenceNode`\n\nContains normalized footnote `id`, display `number`, and optional `referenceIndex` for repeated references.\n\n### `LinkNode`\n\nContains policy-processed `href`, optional `title`, and inline `children`.\n\n### `ImageNode`\n\nContains policy-processed `src`, text `alt`, and optional `title`.\n\n### `BreakNode`\n\nMarker node with `type: 'break'`.\n\n### `HtmlInlineNode`\n\nContains raw inline HTML `value`. It is created only when HTML parsing is enabled.\n\n### `InlineComponentNode`\n\nContains `type: 'inlineComponent'`, `name`, source `attributes`, inline `children`, and optional rendered `tagName` and string `properties`. Uses the same component replacements as `ComponentNode`, with a `<span>` fallback when no tag is provided. See [Custom components](../guides/extensions.md#custom-components).\n\n## Parsing and rendering options\n\n### `ParseOptions`\n\nConfigures `allowHtml`, `urlTransform`, `frontmatter`, `headingIds`, and `extensions`. It also exposes `references`, `footnotes`, `footnoteOrder`, and `footnoteCounts` state used by nested parser contexts.\n\n### `UrlTransform`\n\nSynchronous callback `(url: string, kind: 'link' | 'image', defaultUrl: string) => string | null`. Return the default screened URL, a trusted replacement, or `null` to keep only the label content. Applies during Markdown parsing, not to raw HTML or supplied ASTs. See [Custom URL policy](../core-concepts/security.md#custom-url-policy).\n\n### `RenderOptions`\n\nExtends `ParseOptions` with `highlighter`, `codeLineNumbers`, and `headingAnchors`.\n\n### `CodeHighlighter`\n\nSynchronous callback `(code, lang?, options?) => string`. The returned string is trusted HTML for the contents of `<code>`.\n\n### `CodeHighlightOptions`\n\nContains optional raw fence `meta`, `highlightLines`, and `lineNumbers` passed to a `CodeHighlighter`.\n\n### `HeadingAnchorOptions`\n\nConfigures anchor `content`, `className`, `ariaHidden`, and `tabIndex`.\n\n## Extension contracts\n\n### `MarkdownExtension`\n\nNamed hook object with optional `parseBlock`, `transformDocument`, `transformInline`, and `renderHtml` functions, plus an optional `inlineParser`.\n\n### `BlockParseContext`\n\nProvides source `lines`, current `index`, active `options`, nested `parseInline` and `parseBlocks` helpers, and `consume`.\n\n### `InlineParser`\n\nContains literal starting UTF-16 code-unit `markers` and a synchronous `parse(context)` callback returning `InlineParseResult | undefined`. Runs at matching source positions after escapes and code spans, before other built-in inline rules.\n\n### `InlineParseContext`\n\nProvides current-container `source`, UTF-16 `index`, active `options`, `inLink`, and a nested `parseInline(value)` helper that shares the recursion and scan budget.\n\n### `InlineParseResult`\n\nContains one standard `InlineNode` as `node` and a positive integer `length` in UTF-16 code units. The range must fit in the current source. Invalid lengths throw `RangeError`.\n\n### `InlineTransformContext`\n\nProvides active parse `options` to inline transforms.\n\n### `DocumentTransformContext`\n\nProvides active parse `options` to document transforms.\n\n### `HtmlRenderContext`\n\nProvides active render `options` and recursive `renderBlock` and `renderInline` functions.\n\n## Supporting data\n\n### `MarkdownHeading`\n\nCollected heading data with `id`, `text`, numeric `level`, and optional `framework`.\n\n### `LinkReferenceDefinition`\n\nNormalized reference data with `href` and optional `title`.\n\n### `FootnoteDefinition`\n\nFootnote source data with original `label`, Markdown `content`, and optional generated `id`.\n"}
